## Run

```bash
composer install
cp .env.example .env
php bin/migrate.php                 # create the schema
php -S localhost:4001 public/index.php   # start the server
```

## Layout

```
public/index.php       # front controller — YOURS to extend (written once, never overwritten)
bin/migrate.php        # migration runner (applies pending migrations/*.php in order)
app/Generated/         # owned by Backbone — regenerated wholesale, do not edit
  Config/              # Env loader + shared PDO
  Support/             # Request, Response, CaseMap, exceptions
  Http/                # the router
  Middleware/          # error handler<% if (auth) { %> + JWT auth guard<% } %>
  Models/              # PDO repositories (camelCase API <-> snake_case columns)
  Services/            # business layer
  Controllers/         # request handlers
  Validators/          # per-entity request validation (422 on failure)
<% if (auth) { %>  Auth/                # register / login / me
<% } %>  Routes/routes.php    # the route table
migrations/            # additive, numbered — never edited or deleted
```

Anything under `app/Generated/` is overwritten every time you regenerate. Everything else is
yours. Add custom routes in `public/index.php` where marked.

